2. Dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runtime:

  BepInEx / BepInEx.Unity.IL2CPP (BepInExPack_V_Rising 1.733.2)
    https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx - LGPL-2.1
    The only runtime dependency. Progenitor is a plugin on the BepInEx
    chainloader; it is not a second loader.

  HarmonyX (via BepInEx)
    https://github.com/BepInEx/HarmonyX - MIT
    Used as a library for patching. Progenitor's own hook and event ordering is
    original code that reuses Harmony's *model* (see section 3).

  Il2CppInterop (via BepInEx)
    https://github.com/BepInEx/Il2CppInterop - LGPL-3.0
    Generates the interop assemblies Progenitor compiles against.

Bundled with BepInExPack_V_Rising and used through it (not redistributed here):

  Mono.Cecil (via BepInEx core)
    https://github.com/jbevain/cecil - MIT
    Reads and rewrites plugin assemblies in Bootstrap, the preloader and the
    compatibility rewriter.

  SemanticVersioning (via BepInEx core)
    https://github.com/adamreeve/semver.net - MIT
    BepInEx's plugin version type, referenced by the preloader.

Build only:

  BepInEx.PluginInfoProps 2.1.0 (NuGet)
    https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx.Templates - MIT
    Emits MyPluginInfo. Compile-time only (PrivateAssets=all).

  .NET SDK and runtime libraries (System.Text.Json and the rest of the BCL)
    https://github.com/dotnet/runtime - MIT

  V Rising game assemblies (Stunlock Studios). Referenced from the local install
  as compile-time file references with Private="false". They are NOT
  redistributed by this repository and are not NuGet dependencies. No game
  asset, game binary, interop assembly or native code is committed here.

Tests and development tools only (never shipped in a release package):

  xunit 2.9.3 and xunit.runner.visualstudio 2.8.2
    https://github.com/xunit/xunit - Apache-2.0

  Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.12.0
    https://github.com/microsoft/vstest - MIT

  Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp (Roslyn) 4.8.0
    https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn - MIT
    Used by the test project and tools/enc (method-body deltas).

  Mono.Cecil 0.11.4 (NuGet)
    https://github.com/jbevain/cecil - MIT
    The test project compiles the rewriter sources against the same version
    BepInEx ships, because CI has no game install.

  @modelcontextprotocol/sdk (^1.12.0) and zod (^3.23.8), with their
  transitive npm dependencies as pinned in tools/mcp/package-lock.json
    https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk - MIT
    https://github.com/colinhacks/zod - MIT
    The MCP server in tools/mcp that exposes the development bridge.

  Node.js, Python and Blender are external tools some scripts under tools/
  run on or inside; none of them is included in this repository.

Interoperability data read from the game:

  To work with the game, the source includes a small amount of factual data
  read from the installed game: component and buffer layout constants (field
  offsets, sizes and strides, e.g. src/Progenitor.Core/Layout/), prefab GUID
  hashes and asset names, character rig bone names and reference data, and
  game balance numbers that features match or document. It is included solely
  for interoperability. It is not game code, art or audio, and Stunlock
  Studios retains all rights in the game itself.

