3. Borrowed ideas, with attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Harmony / HarmonyX - https://github.com/pardeike/Harmony
  - The prefix/postfix, integer priority, and before/after-id ordering model,
    reimplemented in original code for the event bus, system hooks and the
    Content.Edit sorter (which inverts the priority direction).
    (Progenitor.Core/Plugins/OrderSorter.cs)

Thunderstore, r2modman and Gale - https://thunderstore.io/
  - Packaging and install conventions for the V Rising community. The
    observation that the public package API carries no checksum is why
    Progenitor's operator-signed catalogue records SHA-256 of the offered
    bytes.

BepInEx ecosystems generally
  - The posture that every plugin runs with full process authority, so the
    mitigations that work are visibility and a small trusted core rather than
    a sandbox.

